# Customers' own domains for published App Studio sites, with certificates issued on demand.
#
# Customers point their domain at this server with a CNAME (NOVARA_SITES_CNAME_TARGET). Before Caddy
# asks a certificate authority for a certificate, it asks NOVARA whether the domain is one a
# customer has proven (DNS TXT record) and whose site is live; anything else gets no certificate,
# so nobody can make this server request certificates for names it doesn't serve.
#
# Run Caddy next to the API (it listens on 80 and 443; the API stays on 127.0.0.1:8000). The API
# serves the site for any proven Host it is given (studio/domains.py), so Caddy only has to pass
# the original Host header through, which reverse_proxy does by default.
{
	on_demand_tls {
		ask http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/public/domains/check
	}
}

https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
